mobileportrait-mlx
==================

An independent MLX reimplementation of MobilePortrait (CVPR 2025), built by
forking and modifying the Thin-Plate-Spline-Motion-Model. This project's own
code is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

It incorporates and builds on the following third-party work; their licenses
and copyrights are retained and apply to their respective portions:

- Thin-Plate-Spline-Motion-Model (the fork base, vendored under reference-tps/)
  https://github.com/yoyo-nb/Thin-Plate-Spline-Motion-Model
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 yoyo-nb. Full text: reference-tps/LICENSE

- First Order Motion Model (FOMM), which TPS itself derives from
  https://github.com/AliaksandrSiarohin/first-order-model
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019 Aliaksandr Siarohin

- MobilePortrait (architecture reference only; no code or weights used)
  "MobilePortrait: Real-Time One-Shot Neural Head Avatars on Mobile Devices",
  Jiang et al., CVPR 2025, arXiv:2407.05712. The architecture is ByteDance's;
  its code and weights are unreleased. This repository is a clean reimplementation
  from the paper, not a copy of any ByteDance source.

Runtime dependencies (not redistributed here, fetched on demand):

- VGG19 perceptual-loss weights via torchvision (BSD-3-Clause).
- InsightFace "buffalo_l" facial-keypoint detector, used as the optional FK
  backend, is downloaded at runtime. InsightFace pretrained models are released
  for NON-COMMERCIAL / research use only — see https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface
  for their terms before any commercial use.

Trained checkpoints are NOT distributed in this repository. Any weights produced
by warm-starting from TPS (VoxCeleb) or training on VoxCeleb / CelebV-HQ inherit
those datasets' research / non-commercial terms.
